8jrc|n|One who, or that which, sets; -- used mostly in composition with a noun, as typesetter; or in combination with an adverb, as a setter on (or inciter), a setter up, a setter forth. ; A hunting dog of a special breed originally derived from a cross between the spaniel and the pointer. Modern setters are usually trained to indicate the position of game birds by standing in a fixed position, but originally they indicated it by sitting or crouching. ; One who hunts victims for sharpers. ; One who adapts words to music in composition. ; An adornment; a decoration; -- with off. ; A shallow seggar for porcelain.	a:90nr,89,162;3nz9,85,2;9cdh,77,154;3b8s,72,1;9cdx,70,1;9cd7,66,9;4rt8,63,13;3pia,51,164;4n6q,43,23;8svl,42,5;4o2f,39,2;4fhk,38,15;6szj,34,38;82wl,31,1;4lq6,31,284~7j6e,7,796;22ah,27,784;7ex5,21,726;4lq6,31,284;6tfq,3,222;3pia,51,164;90nr,89,162;9cdh,77,154;hay,14,128;1vsq,14,106;5h97,19,93;969d,3,80;4kkj,6,74;7hnv,8,70;3lxf,2,70	v:9cdx,80,2;9cdh,74,122;9cd7,63,7;4o2f,29,1;4rt8,26,1;4p40,24,4;5rm1,22,3;6t05,18,24;3pia,17,15;4nzl,13,1;18ag,11,147;7hnv,9,75;7cjb,6,1;3lxf,5,88;4k4f,5,1~18ag,11,147;9cdh,74,122;3lxf,5,88;7hnv,9,75;6t05,18,24;3pia,17,15;9cd7,63,7;4p40,24,4;5rm1,22,3;9cdx,80,2;4nzl,13,1;4rt8,26,1;4o2f,29,1;7cjb,6,1;1tm8,2,1	V:6m64,50,4;805h,40,25;9ur4,38,4;9cdh,36,9;6tef,33,4;oo9,24,1;6m5b,23,29;18dj,12,132;3p6h,6,154~3p6h,6,154;18dj,12,132;6m5b,23,29;805h,40,25;9cdh,36,9;9ur4,38,4;6m64,50,4;6tef,33,4;oo9,24,1	n:3cnd,97,7;3b8s,88,3;3nz9,75,1;3pia,72,723;5rqo,72,3;82wl,54,5;52gg,52,7;2pwu,50,2;9jg4,49,9;8je4,47,6;7h3q,42,2642;8ut4,42,7;95qw,41,6;1osp,40,2;2pxn,37,1~7h3q,42,2642;3pia,72,723;abv8,10,273;969d,13,155;mth,6,96;2cjg,0,59;1umw,12,40;8jrc,20,36;7u6d,15,35;4hqz,16,34;129b,18,28;ego,24,21;8051,8,17;9neg,8,16;6ttc,29,11	N:5rke,86,6;4bkc,80,12;5rli,73,8;4hqz,60,686;3vmq,54,3;5rnv,54,3980;3pia,51,167;8j4g,47,1;1xi,47,44;5rkf,41,6279;2937,37,1316;5rle,36,4;4hr6,35,10;28qm,32,6;8je4,31,2~5rkf,41,6279;5rnv,54,3980;2937,37,1316;3iqq,5,1027;4hqz,60,68